Subject: [PATCH 28/29] fix(glitch): re-freeze the live180/edge179/glyph178
 milestone hashes

Same class as the just-fixed task35/edge/glyph-map/emboss re-freezes:
this milestone chain's exclusion set is identical in composition to
edge_bvec3_contour's and emboss_color_style's (same corpus-bump-changed
programs riding into the projection, now also carrying the post-integ4-
merge MRT/julia/texture-driver emitter changes).

Cross-validated rather than recomputed blind: edge179 and glyph178 here
share the exact same program-set composition as the just-verified
edge_bvec3_contour/glyph_map_nonnegative_int_shift/emboss_color_style
values, so I reused those (byte-identical, not re-derived independently
-- but this test's own internal self-consistency checks, which compare
live180/edge179/glyph178 directly against EACH OTHER rather than any
frozen value, already passed before this fix and continue to). Only
"live180" (glitch included, one level "younger" than edge179) needed a
fresh generate_outputs call; its result came back byte-identical to
emboss_color_style's independently-derived "glitch180" state (same
milestone under a different chain's naming), a second independent
confirmation.

All 13 tests pass (Ran 13 tests ... OK).

